Host-side gtest unit tests for crosspoint-reader.

Build and run:

  cmake -S test -B build/test
  cmake --build build/test
  ctest --test-dir build/test --output-on-failure -j

Run a single suite directly:

  cmake --build build/test --target StreamingJsonParserTest
  build/test/streaming_json_parser/StreamingJsonParserTest --gtest_filter='*'

Google Test is fetched via CMake FetchContent on first configure; the pinned
version lives in test/CMakeLists.txt.

Three targets here are host tools, not gtest suites, so ctest does not run them:

  map_preview  renders a map frame with the device's own MapRenderer --
               docs/device-preview.md (parent repo)
  map_replay   replays a recorded ride through the device's own
               MapFollow::decide() and counts redraws, with a threshold sweep
               -- docs/map-follow.md, "Sweeping the thresholds off the device"
  wallet_preview
               renders a generated wallet asset through the device's own
               WalletAsset/ManifestParser code and writes PNGs of the
               framebuffer -- docs/wallet-viewer.md, "Read against real
               generator output". `pio run -t wallet-preview`.
               `--code N` renders a machine-readable code and reports its hash,
               module box, centring and label band -- same doc, "The code
               screen". `--key <64 hex>` renders an ENCRYPTED tree: GCM tag
               first, then AES-256-CTR per asset -- docs/wallet-crypto.md.
               `--grey` renders the level's grey asset as four visible levels,
               cross-checks the baked planes against the 2bpp image, and writes
               <out>-capture.bin -- the exact CMD:SCREENSHOT_GRAY payload for that
               window, which tools/greyshot.py decodes off-device;
               `--synth-grey DIR` writes a synthetic grey tree to render --
               docs/wallet-grey.md
